    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d338-a1">

                <pb facs="0321" n="301" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg301"/>

                <head>Mr. Harrington to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Treasury Department,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-08-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 18, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    letter of August 11, enclosing a copy of a communication from Mr. De Stoeckl,
                    minister of Russia, <pb facs="0322" n="302" xml:id="pg302"/> who inquires
                    whether persons of Russian birth, who have been naturalized as American citizens
                    and subsequently returned to Russia, are required to pay any impost in order to
                    obtain the privilege of exporting their property.</p>
                <p>In reply I have to state that there is no law imposing any such tax as that
                    referred to.</p>
                <p>With great respect,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEO. HARRINGTON, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary of the
                            Treasury.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
